Use EntryPoint's nonce validation (ERC-4337 spec):

IEntryPoint public immutable entryPoint;

function validateUserOp(...) external {
uint192 key = uint192(userOp.nonce >> 64);

// ✅ Use EntryPoint's getNonce (enforces sequential nonces)
uint256 expectedNonce = entryPoint.getNonce(address(this), key);
require(userOp.nonce == expectedNonce, "Invalid nonce");

// EntryPoint automatically increments nonce
}

Benefits:
- Sequential nonce enforcement
- Unique userOpHash guarantee
- Standard compliant

